% :index changes how rules are pre-filtered before matching, never what a
% program computes. Here the second argument (depth 1) is indexed instead
% of the default first one.

data color.
symb red, green, blue color.

:index (2) "Hash"
pred name-of int, color -> string.
name-of _ red "red".
name-of _ green "green".
name-of _ blue "blue".

main :- name-of 1 green S, print S.
